Quotes
We have two quotes that are single quotes and double quotes.
When our input have special characters and we need to disable the speciality of those special characters then we need to approach for quotes.

Single quotes are strict quoting.
Whereas Double quotes give you a leniency to access the variables in them.
So it is a choice to pick which one to use.

example

x=200
echo $x

echo '**** $x *****'  #we go with single quotes when we wanted to print what is inside of echo.

echo "**** $x *****"   # it will print the variable value so always go with double quotes
